Adding readme, will update later. This is a dungeon crawler game, I'm planning on working on this iteratively over a longer period. The name is a placeholder until I come up with a better name, right now this is just a rough idea in my head so expect a lot to change over the next few commits.

Windows build (MSYS2 UCRT64)
---------------------------
Put C:\msys64\ucrt64\bin first on PATH, ahead of other MinGW installations.
Install the native UCRT64 tools and graphics dependency from an MSYS2 terminal:

    pacman -S --needed mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-gcc mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-cmake mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-ninja mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-freetype

From the project root in PowerShell:

    cmake --preset ucrt64-debug
    cmake --build --preset ucrt64-debug
    cd cmake-build-ucrt64-debug
    .\Dungeon_Crawler.exe

Use ucrt64-release instead of ucrt64-debug for a Release build.
The first configure downloads SFML 2.6.2 from its official repository and builds
it with UCRT64 GCC, using UCRT64 FreeType. The game still uses the SFML 2 API;
the MSYS2 SFML 3 package cannot replace it. SFML DLLs are copied beside the game;
keep UCRT64 bin on PATH for the compiler and FreeType runtime dependencies.
Player assets resolve from the project's assets directory regardless of the
launch working directory. If sprites/player.png is absent, the player uses the
checked-in Missing_Texture.png placeholder. The world renderer is still disabled
in the game loop. The recovered MagicLand.tmx experiment references
magiclanddizzy_tiles.gif, which was missing from the original archive.

In CLion, reload CMake presets and select MSYS2 UCRT64 Debug or Release.
If CLion overrides the preset tools, set its MinGW toolchain location to
C:\msys64\ucrt64, CMake to C:\msys64\ucrt64\bin\cmake.exe, and the build tool
to C:\msys64\ucrt64\bin\ninja.exe.
The presets use fresh build folders. The legacy cmake-build-debug cache was
created for an old project location and the bundled CLion compiler.

For another MSYS2 location, create a local CMakeUserPresets.json that inherits
one of these presets and overrides MSYS2_UCRT64_ROOT and the PATH environment.
An existing SFML 2.6 installation built with the same toolchain can be used with
-DDUNGEON_USE_SYSTEM_SFML=ON and -DSFML_DIR=<prefix>/lib/cmake/SFML.
